        <tr><td><a href="../../lessons/6.2.html">6.2</a></td><td>Ground Checks: No Infinite Jumps</td><td>raycast, layer masks, re-derived state</td></tr>
        <tr><td><a href="../../lessons/6.3.html">6.3</a></td><td>Jump Feel: Fall Speed &amp; Coyote Time</td><td>asymmetric gravity, buffer, coyote — feel engineering</td></tr>
        <tr><td><a href="../../lessons/6.4.html">6.4</a></td><td>Boots: Double Jump</td><td>jump counters, capability design, soft gates</td></tr>
        <tr><td><a href="../../lessons/6.5.html">6.5</a></td><td>Platforming Studio: The Gauntlet</td><td>five sections, one room, blind testers</td></tr>
</table>

<h2>Concepts this unit owns</h2>
<p><strong>Feel as engineering</strong>: every "tight" jump is three tunable numbers with names. Also the raycast — asking physics a question per frame — and the counter-vs-bool data decision. CED: AAP-3, DAT-1 (the tuning data), CRD-1.</p>

